<title>SWITZERLAND: UBS says staff costs rise 17 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>UBS says staff costs rise 17 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union Bank of Switzerland (UBS) said on Friday personnel costs rose 17 percent in 1996 to 4,857 million Swiss francs due largely to performance bonuses.</p>
<p>&quot;This increase was due in large part to performance- and profit-related bonuses, which were considerably higher than in 1995 due to UBS's good operating results,&quot; the bank said in a statement before a news conference.</p>
<p>UBS said its staff numbers in Switzerland decreased by 499 while staff outside Switzerland rose by 581 in 1996.</p>
<p>&quot;At the end of 1996 UBS employed a staff of 29,153 worldwide, 7,682 of these outside Switzerland,&quot; UBS said.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
